// @test regression/INV138-scalar-receiver-no-false-positive
// @description The two escape hatches that keep the INV138 scalar-receiver check FP-safe, both TV-clean (probed p06, 2026-07-15). A user `method` on a scalar type makes `a.getType()` legal, including via overloads on several scalar types. `declaredFunctionNames` is name-only (it does not match the overload signature), which is deliberately over-lenient - it must never flag a name a user method owns. The imported-library hatch is pinned separately by INV138-imported-method-on-scalar.
// @expects parse: success
// @expects errors: 0
//@version=6
indicator("x")
method getType(int this) =>
    na(this) ? "int(na)" : "int"
method getType(float this) =>
    na(this) ? "float(na)" : "float"
method getType(string this) =>
    na(this) ? "string(na)" : "string"
a = 1
b = 1.0
e = "1"
results = str.format("a: {0}\nb: {1}\ne: {2}", a.getType(), b.getType(), e.getType())
var label lbl = label.new(0, 0)
lbl.set_x(bar_index)
lbl.set_text(results)
